INT. SLOANE'S APARTMENT — BEDROOM — EARLY EVENING

[[ENTER: SLOANE]]
[[WARDROBE: SLOANE: WD-SLOANE-HOUSE-GE92]]

Three looks lie across the bed. SLOANE LOCKWOOD (33), hair already finished, holds the first against herself at the mirror, steps into it, and spins. The skirt follows half a beat late, like it's being polite.

[[TIME: 5]]

The second look. She spins. Nothing moves at all. She stops mid-turn and regards herself with real disappointment.

[[TIME: 4]]

SLOANE
(to the mirror)
If I can't dance in it, it's a costume.

She drops it on top of the first and picks up the third.

[[TIME: 2]]

Half-dressed in the third, a robe over her shoulders, she sits on the end of the bed with a slice of coconut cake. Her makeup brushes wait, untouched, on the dresser.

[[TIME: 5]]
[[PROP: PR-COCONUT-CAKE: on a plate in Sloane's hand]]

On the windowsill, a fern in a handsome pot is dying with great dignity. A brown frond lets go and drops. Sloane leans toward it, fork still in hand.

[[TIME: 4]]
[[PROP: PR-FERN: windowsill, one frond fallen]]

SLOANE
(softly, to the fern)
Sorry, darling. I believe in you.

[[FREEZE: SLOANE LOCKWOOD.]]

SLOANE (V.O.)
I can get anyone into any room in this city. I can't keep a fern alive.

Later. The robe is gone. She stands at the mirror in the third look, chin up, fighting the clasp of her necklace. The cake plate sits on the dresser beside her.

[[TIME: 4]]
[[WARDROBE: SLOANE: WD-SLOANE-PARTY-GE92]]
[[PROP: PR-COCONUT-CAKE: on the dresser, within reach]]
[[SFX: A key in the front door. No knock.]]
[[ENTER: GIDEON]]
[[WARDROBE: GIDEON: WD-GIDEON-SUIT]]

GIDEON SHAW (44) lets himself in with his own key and appears in the bedroom doorway. He takes in the clothes on the bed without comment.

[[TIME: 3]]

SLOANE
(not turning around)
You could knock.

GIDEON
I could.

He crosses to her, takes the two ends of the chain from her fingers, and fastens the clasp. She lowers her hands and lets him.

[[TIME: 4]]
[[PROP: PR-SLOANE-NECKLACE: fastened by Gideon]]

She reaches for the cake. He lifts the plate out from under her fork and sets it on top of the wardrobe, out of her reach.

[[TIME: 3]]
[[PROP: PR-COCONUT-CAKE: on top of the wardrobe, out of reach]]

SLOANE
I wasn't finished.

GIDEON
You were.

She sits at the dresser and does her makeup fast and well. Then she touches her hair. Then she touches it again.

[[TIME: 4]]
[[EXIT: GIDEON]]
[[EXIT: SLOANE]]

INT. SLOANE'S APARTMENT — DOORWAY — EARLY EVENING

[[ENTER: GIDEON]]
[[ENTER: SLOANE]]

Gideon holds the front door. Sloane sweeps past the hall table and scoops up her clutch, one hand still at her hair.

[[TIME: 3]]
[[PROP: PR-SLOANE-CLUTCH: in Sloane's hand]]

GIDEON
Car's downstairs. Your hair's perfect. Stop touching it.

She takes her hand off her hair, grins at him, and goes.

[[TIME: 2]]

CUT TO:
